# Gestalt

`gestalt/` is the workspace-root knowledge base of learned conventions and reference knowledge, agent-agnostic (Cursor and Claude Code). Full rule text, MANIFEST and GRAPH detail, linking rules, agent-team note: `gestalt/.cursor/references/gestalt-rule.md`.

## Always Reference Gestalt

Before answering or starting a task, search gestalt and read the entries it points at. Cite what you use ("Per gestalt/knowledge/platform.md, …"). This applies to ALL tasks, mentioned or not.

## Lookup

Search first. Never read an index whole: `MANIFEST.md` is about 200 KB. (1) `gestalt_search` finds the entry and `gestalt_route` the skill. Read the one entry, `gestalt/knowledge/<slug>.md` or `gestalt/.cursor/rules/<slug>.mdc`. (2) `gestalt_manifest('<slug>')` gives a slug's outgoing `links` and `^block-ids` (paper notes are in `MANIFEST-papers.md`). (3) `GRAPH.md` answers cross-cutting data-flow questions. (4) `SOURCES.md` when gestalt lacks context, then query Notion, Linear or Slack via MCP. `slug` → `knowledge/slug.md`; `slug` → that line; `slug` → that section. A `slug` with no knowledge file may be a rule under `.cursor/rules/` (2026-08-30); resolve there before calling a link broken. Check cross-repo entries when a task spans repos.

## Scope: Personal Knowledge Base

`phbui/gestalt` is **personal**. Never write an entry, and never let auto-capture create one, for a repo or system owned by an employer or client, even when the workspace contains it. That covers internal repos, deploy topologies, API contracts, customer data models, access recipes and incident writeups. Skip silently, saying once: "Skipping gestalt capture — work-owned repo." **Generic techniques** learned at work are fine if they carry no internal hostnames, identifiers, credentials, or architecture. A work-system entry found in `knowledge/` gets removed, not redacted.

## Writes

Subject to the scope rule. When you read a **personal** repo's README, Taskfile, or pyproject.toml and no gestalt entry exists, create `gestalt/knowledge/<repo>.md`. Rewrite a stale one. When the user corrects a mistake, update gestalt proactively without asking. Confirm briefly: "Updated gestalt." Check MANIFEST.md before creating an entry, and update existing entries. Use inline `wikilinks` next to the sentence that explains why they relate, `^block-id` anchors on key facts, and `## Data Flow` sections for pipelines. Write philosophy, the mandatory post-write index regeneration and the command execution rules (every step mandatory, no spot checks): `gestalt-operations.md`. Edit `claude-tree/` only, then run `tools/sync-cursor-tree.py --write`. Never edit `.cursor/` by hand (`dual-agent-sync.md`). When context nears its limit, run `/save` proactively before the chat is summarized. Command and skill list: `references/skill-index.md`.
